      "widgets_values": [
        "A single continuous 3.04-second 2D illustrated fantasy game warm laughing reaction. The adult illustrated woman Mara from <Picture 1> is alone at the same wooden tavern counter throughout. Preserve her exact green eyes, red hair and single thick braid over the shoulder on the left of the image, teal scarf and cape, burgundy leather bodice with gold fastenings, rolled white sleeves, brown fingerless gloves, belt, dark trousers, jewelry and two turquoise bottles. Keep the exact drawn face, proportions, clothing coverage, colored outlines and painted cel shading. She reacts with a short spontaneous warm chuckle. Her smile opens naturally and her eyes soften almost closed with amusement. Two small connected shoulder and upper-torso pulses accompany the brief laugh, with only a tiny forward inclination as one coherent unit. Keep the movement gentle and readable rather than a large bow or repeated rocking. Her head follows naturally with stable neck length. Both of her own hands remain laid comfortably on their original places on the counter; her forearms and elbows support the small torso movement naturally. Fingers and thumbs keep their original relaxed shapes. Small natural follow-through of her clothing and braid follows the connected laughing impulses with a slight delay and settles quickly with her body. No isolated movement while at rest. Keep her original body shape and clothing coverage. She finishes the chuckle, reopens her eyes and returns to her original small closed-mouth smile. Start and finish in the exact supplied counter stance, with both of her own hands resting at their original places on the wooden counter, open eyes and the original small closed-mouth smile. Keep natural neck length and comfortable original chin-to-scarf spacing. The head follows the small body movement naturally and never slides or sinks into the shoulders. Both hands belong to Mara; no other person appears. Preserve the original relaxed finger shape and thumb position, with all fingers stable relative to their palm. The camera, framing, counter, tavern furniture and warm lighting remain completely fixed. The countertop and all existing props remain unchanged. All originally open space above the counter and around her stays empty; the existing counter remains fully intact. Nothing enters or leaves the frame. Keep the original illustrated game artwork throughout. No speaking, lip sync, captions, music or sound.",
        480,
        704,
        73
      ]
